title: StartDay3
position: -125,-487
---
<<set $daysPassed = 681>>
<<play_sound AlarmClock>>
<<play_music MainTheme>>
<<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
I wake to the alarm again. My body knows the routine now. The ache, the fog, the slow reassembly of self.
Cryosleep doesn't get easier. You just get better at pretending it does.
I blink at the mission clock.
Day {$daysPassed}.
The ship smells the same. The silence sounds the same. But something in my chest has shifted.
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
I know there's someone out there. And they know I'm here. The thought still carries warmth, even after the ice.
<<else>>
I know there's someone out there. And they know I'm here.
<<endif>>
<<show_ui ClickToInteract>>
<<show MonitorOffDay3>>
===

title: OnClickedMonitorDay3
position: -128,-338
---
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
I power on the monitor. The usual HQ digest loads. Mission parameters unchanged, supply inventory nominal, another reminder about reporting protocols.
But underneath the routine, the comms buffer has a new entry.
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
A single packet, tagged with {$catName}'s frequency. The translator renders it into a short burst.
<<speed 0.4>>
<<play_sound RobotStillHere 0.25>>
"STILL HERE" <i>[12 DAYS AGO]</i>
<<speed 1>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
Two words, sent while I was frozen. A reminder that patience doesn't require a heartbeat.
Something in my chest loosens. They waited. Again.
I press the response key and send a ping back. Two can be patient.
The day still needs a shape, but at least the silence has a crack in it now.
    -> (start the day)
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
<<else>>
Two words. Twelve days ago.
I note the timestamp and close the buffer. I'll deal with that later. For now, the day needs a shape.
    -> (start the day)
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
<<endif>>
===

title: RegularTasksDay3
position: 260,308
---
<<once>>
<<declare $day3DidPushups = false>>
<<declare $day3DidStargaze = false>>
<<declare $day3DidSystemsCheck = false>>
<<endonce>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
The ship hums beneath me. I have time before anything demands my attention.
My body is stiff from cryosleep. My mind is restless. I should do something with both.
    -> (do some push-ups) <<if $day3DidPushups == false>>
        <<set $day3DidPushups = true>>
        I drop to the floor. The count is slower today, my arms heavier, but the rhythm is still mine.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        By the end I'm breathing hard, but I feel more present in my own skin.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
    -> (stare at the stars) <<if $day3DidStargaze == false>>
        <<set $day3DidStargaze = true>>
        I press my face close to the viewport and let the stars fill my vision until there's no room for anything else.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        For a few minutes, the loneliness fades into something closer to wonder.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
    -> (check the ship systems) <<if $day3DidSystemsCheck == false>>
        <<set $day3DidSystemsCheck = true>>
        I pull up the diagnostics panel. Life support, comms, power draw. All within tolerance.
        One line catches my eye. Long-term oxygen reserves are slightly below projected baseline. Not critical. Not yet.
        I make a mental note and move on.
        <<jump RegularTasksDay3>>
    -> (move on)
        <<jump PrepareReportDay3>>
===

title: PrepareReportDay3
position: 259,417
---
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
I sit down at the terminal. The report template blinks at me, the same empty fields I've filled a hundred times.
Before I can type the first word, the comms panel lights up.
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
<<show MonitorSilhouette>>
{$catName}'s frequency. Live this time, not a recording.
    -> (answer)
        <<jump CallCatDay3>>
    -> (ignore it and write the report first)
        I try to focus on the report. The cursor blinks. The frequency pulses.
        I last about thirty seconds.
            -> (answer)
        <<jump CallCatDay3>>
===

title: CallCatDay3
position: 422,282
---
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
<<hide MonitorOn>>
<<show MonitorSilhouette>>
<<show_character Cat Obscure right>>
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
I open the channel. Static, then motion. The silhouette leans in, sharper than before, like the translator is getting better at rendering it.
<<play_music CatTheme 0.5>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
    <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
    {$catName}: You came back!
    {$catName}: I practice more word while you gone. Listen. "It is good to see you."
    {$catName}: Did I say right?
        -> Perfect.
            <<positive_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
            <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
            {$catName}: I practice that one many time.
        -> Close enough.
            <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
            {$catName}: I take it. Close is still closer than before.
<<else>>
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
    <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
    {$catName}: Oh. You answer. I was not sure you would.
        -> Of course.
            <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
            {$catName}: Okay. Good.
<<endif>>
<<jump CatConvoDay3>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3
position: 647,285
---
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: So! I have been saving questions for you. Many questions. You ready?
    -> Hit me.
        <<show_character Cat Angry right>>
        {$catName}: Hit you? No! I ask question, not throw thing!
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: ...Oh. That is expression. Okay. I learn that one.
    -> Go for it.
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        {$catName}: Good! I been waiting long time for this.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: Okay! Your ship. It have window, yes? What you see right now?
    -> Stars. Lots of them. What do you see from your window?
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        {$catName}: Stars! I see them too! But from ground. I wonder if we ever look at same one at same time.
        {$catName}: I like that idea. Two people, very far, looking at same tiny light.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: From my window... I see the sky change color three time in one day. Morning is orange, midday is white, and evening is... no word in your language. Deeper than purple.
        {$catName}: And the ground glow a little at night. Soft, like everything remembering the sun.
    -> Mostly just... dark.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: Dark. Yes. Space is very good at dark.
        {$catName}: But dark not mean empty. I am in the dark too, and I am here.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: Next question! Do humans have... pets? Creature that live with you just because?
{$catName}: We have something like that. Small soft thing that hum when you hold it. We call it... no word in your language. But it make you feel less alone.
    -> Yeah, we have dogs and cats. What's yours like?
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        {$catName}: Cat! I remember you say this word. The cat look like me? I hope cat look like me.
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: Mine is small, round, very warm. It not have face exactly... more like a feeling with a shape. When I hold it, it hum and the hum go into your chest.
        {$catName}: I not seen it in long time though. It stay with my family now.
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
    -> Not on this ship.
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: No pet on ship? That seem... cruel. Everyone need something soft nearby.
        <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The signal holds. {$catName} is still there, leaning forward on screen, ready for more.
    -> My turn. I have questions too.
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        {$catName}: You have questions? For me? Ask! Ask!
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_PlayerQuestions>>
    -> (keep talking)
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_Montage>>
    -> (end the conversation)
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_End>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3_PlayerQuestions
position: 647,340
---
<<once>>
<<declare $d3AskedFriends = false>>
<<declare $d3AskedPlanet = false>>
<<declare $d3AskedSleep = false>>
<<endonce>>
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    -> Do you have friends on your planet? <<if $d3AskedFriends == false>>
        <<set $d3AskedFriends = true>>
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: Friends...
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: I have people I see. People I sit near. But they all follow the rules very careful. They not say what they really think.
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: I try once, when I was younger. I tell someone I think the rules too strict. They look at me like I say something broken.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: After that I stop trying. Easier to be alone than to be wrong in company.
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: But you... you not look at me like that. That is why this feel different.
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_PlayerQuestions>>
    -> What's it like outside on your planet? <<if $d3AskedPlanet == false>>
        <<set $d3AskedPlanet = true>>
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: Oh! It is beautiful. The air is thick and warm. It taste like something sweet, but not sugar. More like... the feeling of sweet?
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: The ground is soft in most place. Not like rock. More like... if moss was alive and breathing. It move a little under your feet.
        {$catName}: And the light! The light not come from one place like your sun. It come from everywhere. The sky, the ground, even the water glow.
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        {$catName}: At night, when everything dim, you can hear the planet hum. Low and deep, like it sleeping.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_PlayerQuestions>>
    -> What do you think about right before you fall asleep? <<if $d3AskedSleep == false>>
        <<set $d3AskedSleep = true>>
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: Hmm. That is... very interesting question.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: I think about... whether tomorrow will be different. 
        {$catName}: Usually it is not... but I still hope.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: And lately... I think about what you doing. If you dreaming in your ice box. If you dreaming about me.
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        {$catName}: That is silly, I know. But it make falling asleep easier.
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_PlayerQuestions>>
    -> (stop asking questions)
        <<jump CatConvoDay3_Montage>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3_Montage
position: 647,575
---
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
And just like last time, the conversation keeps going. Easier now. Like a path we've walked before.
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: ...no, you not understand. The fruit is not red. It is the color AFTER red. Your eyes just cannot see it!
    -> ...
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: ...so your planet has frozen water that fall from sky AND liquid water that fall from sky? How you know which one is coming?
    -> ...
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
{$catName}: ...and then the little creature just sit on my hand! Not afraid at all! I think it like the warmth.
    -> ...
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: ...Oh! Oh! I learn joke in your language. Ready? Okay. Okay.
{$catName}: Why did the star go to school?
<<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
{$catName}: Because it want to be... brighter!
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: ...Why you not laughing? That is very good joke. I practice many time.
    -> ...
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: ...But out here, on this frequency, it is just us. No rules. No watchers. It is only place I feel like... me.
    -> ...
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
The hours slip by without either of us noticing. It's becoming a pattern... the kind of ease that makes you forget there's a vast, empty void between you.
But somewhere underneath the comfort, I notice something. 
The topics come a little slower now. The pauses between them stretch a beat longer than they used to.
<<else>>
The conversation runs longer than I expected. Not bad, exactly. Just... thinner. Like we're both reaching for the next thing to say and finding fewer options each time.
It's still more than I have with anyone else. That has to count for something.
<<endif>>
<<jump CatConvoDay3_SkyGlimpse>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3_SkyGlimpse
position: 647,610
---
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
{$catName}: Oh! I want show you something. Hold on.
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The screen flickers. For a brief moment, the silhouette shifts and I catch a glimpse of a 2D projection of something else.
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1>>
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<show GnarpPlanet>>
They show me a window, with an amber sky and shapes that might be trees, or might be something I have no word for.
It lasts two seconds. Then the feed stabilizes back to the usual framing.
<<fade_transition 2>>
<<wait 1>>
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
<<hide GnarpPlanet>>
{$catName}: That was my sky. I wanted you to see it. Even just little bit.
    -> It's beautiful.
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        {$catName}: It is.
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        Something about that gesture makes me feel less far from everything.
<<endif>>
<<jump CatConvoDay3_End>>
===

title: CatConvoDay3_End
position: 647,630
---
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
The conversation settles into a comfortable lull. Neither of us seems to want to hang up.
<<else>>
The conversation thins out. Neither of us hangs up, but neither of us reaches for the next thing to say either.
<<endif>>
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: Can I tell you something? Something I been carrying for long time?
{$catName}: I need to say it to someone. And you are... only someone I have.
    -> Of course.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        {$catName}: Okay. Thank you.
    -> ...
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: When I was young... a human come to our planet. First one ever.
{$catName}: It was... big thing. Huge thing. Everyone talking about it. The elders, the families, everyone.
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: Some people say, this is good. New life. New knowledge. We should welcome.
{$catName}: Others say, no. Outside life is threat. We not know what they want. We should be afraid.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: My father was in second group. He very afraid. He say humans are... unpredictable. Dangerous. He want the human gone.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: But I was young and curious. I watch the human from far away. I not supposed to, but I do anyway.
{$catName}: He was... clumsy. Tall. Always bumping into thing because gravity different for him. He knock over a whole table once and look so embarrassed.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: But he was kind. He try to learn our words, even though his mouth not made for them. He sound terrible. But he keep trying.
{$catName}: He sit with people and listen. Really listen. Not just wait for his turn to talk.
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: The debates got worse. The people who afraid, they start winning. More and more say the human should leave.
{$catName}: And one day... he was gone. I not know if he left or if they make him leave. Nobody tell me. I was too young to ask the right questions.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: After that, everything change. The afraid people, they make the rules now. No outside contact. No signals. No trust.
{$catName}: That is world I grow up in. World built on fear of one human who come and went.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: But I remember him, {$catThinksPlayerNameIs}. I remember watching him sit in the garden and listen to the wind like it was talking to him.
{$catName}: And I think... my people are wrong. Not because they scared. Being scared make sense. But because they took one person and made him into a monster. They made all humans into that monster.
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: I think there is goodness in humans. Real goodness. I saw it. I was small, but I saw it.
{$catName}: And talking to you... it prove me right. You are not monster. You are just person. Tired, lonely person. Like me.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: My people would say I am naive. That I am making same mistake they made before.
{$catName}: But I think the mistake was not trusting. The mistake was stopping.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: You know what I remember most about him? Small thing. Silly, maybe.
{$catName}: He had this... habit. When he was thinking, or when he look sad, he would hold something small in his hand. Metal, I think. And he would turn it over and over, rubbing the edges with his thumb.
{$catName}: I never see it up close. But I remember the way he hold it. Like it was the last piece of somewhere else.
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
<<stop_music>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show_character Cat Obscure right>>
<<set $negSelfPerception += 2>>
...Dad?
The word surfaces before I can stop it. Not out loud.
A brass compass with a bat etched into the lid. It sat on my father's desk my entire childhood. 
I used to watch him do exactly that... turn it in his hands, thumb tracing the edges, eyes somewhere I couldn't follow.
The sixth expedition was headed for the dark spot. {$catName}'s planet isn't on that route. If that was him... what was he doing there? Did he detour? Did the mission go wrong before he ever reached the star?
How long was he there? What did he see? What did he do that made an entire civilization afraid of humans?
And if he left... or was forced out... where did he go next?
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: {$catThinksPlayerNameIs}?
{$catName}: ...You are okay?
{$catName}: You not saying anything. Did I say something wrong?
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
<<play_music MainTheme>>
I close the channel.
No goodbye. No explanation. Just the click of the connection severing and then silence.
I sit there. Hands on the console. Not moving.
It was him. The compass. The fidgeting. The clumsiness. The listening.
My father was on {$catName}'s planet.
He was supposed to be heading for the dark spot. Straight line, no detours. That was the mission. That was the whole point.
But he stopped. He landed on a world full of people who'd never seen a human, and he stayed long enough for a child to remember his hands.
Why? What was he doing there? What made him leave his mission, leave us, for a garden on a planet nobody's ever heard of?
And what happened to him after? Did he leave? Did they make him leave? Did he ever reach the dark spot, or was that the end of the road?
I don't have answers. I just have a compass on a desk I'll never sit at again, and a story from someone who was too young to ask the right questions.
And somewhere in the static, {$catName} is wondering why I hung up.
<<jump AfterCatLeavesDay3>>
===

title: AfterCatLeavesDay3
position: 915,224
---
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
I push back from the desk. The chair scrapes against the floor, too loud in the silence.
<<if $negSelfPerception >= $posSelfPerception + 3>>
    <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
    It was him. I know it was him. I can feel it like a bruise I didn't know I had until someone pressed on it.
    My father sat in that garden. My father knocked over that table. My father held that compass and thought about us while an entire civilization decided he was a threat.
    And then he vanished. Again.
    The worst part isn't not knowing what happened to him. The worst part is that I'm not surprised. He was always leaving. He just finally found a place far enough away that nobody could follow.
<<elseif $negSelfPerception > $posSelfPerception>>
    <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
    The thought won't settle. It keeps circling, like something caught in orbit.
    What was he doing there? He was supposed to be heading for the dark spot. Straight line, no detours, no stops. That was the mission.
    But he stopped. He sat in a garden. He learned words his mouth wasn't built for. He stayed long enough for a child to remember his hands.
    I don't know what that means. I don't know if it makes him more human or less of a father.
<<else>>
    The pieces are all there. I just can't make them fit into anything that doesn't hurt.
    He detoured. He landed on a planet full of people who'd never seen a human. He was kind to them, and they drove him away anyway.
    And somewhere in the middle of all that, he held a compass with a bat on it and thought about... what? Us? Home? Whether he'd ever go back?
    I'll never know. But the question is lodged in me now, and I don't think it's coming out.
<<endif>>
<<jump EndDay3>>
===

title: EndDay3
position: 918,14
---
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<show PCRoom>>
I don't bother turning the monitor off properly. I just let it go dark on its own.
The report sits unfinished. HQ will get a blank day from me. They can add it to the long list of things I'm failing at.
I climb into the cryopod without ceremony. No routine, no checklist, no pretending I'm fine.
Just the hum of the pod, the cold settling in, and the image behind my eyelids... A man sitting in a garden on a planet he doesn't belong to, turning something small and metal in his hands.
<<fade_transition 3>>
<<wait 2>>
<<jump DreamDay3>>
===

title: DreamDay3
position: 915,500
---
<<stop_music>>
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show BlackHole1>>
The dream starts at the viewport.
The star is there, brighter than it should be, filling the glass like a searchlight. And at its center, the dark spot. The hole that swallowed six expeditions and my father with them.
In the dream, I'm closer than I should be. Much closer. The ship is moving faster than physics should allow, drawn forward as if the dark spot is breathing me in.
I try to check the instruments but they're blank. Every screen, every readout, just black glass reflecting my face back at me.
<<show BlackHole2>>
The dark spot grows. It stops looking like a blemish on a star and starts looking like a mouth. The light around it bends, stretches, thins into threads that spiral inward and vanish.
A black hole. It was always a black hole.
The ship groans. The hull flexes. I feel the pull in my chest, not pain exactly, but a certainty. A direction I can't refuse.
<<show BlackHole3>>
The stars outside begin to streak, then smear, then disappear entirely. The viewport fills with nothing. Pure, total nothing.
    -> (reach toward it)
        I don't fight it. My hand lifts toward the glass, and the darkness reaches back.
        <<if $posSelfPerception > $negSelfPerception>>
            <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
            And just before the black swallows everything, I feel something I didn't expect. Peace. Not the empty kind. The kind that comes from finally letting go of the need to steer.
            Maybe the dark spot isn't an ending. Maybe it's just a door I haven't learned to see through yet.
        <<else>>
            <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
            The darkness takes me without resistance. I was always heading here. Every choice, every report, every sleepless night was just a longer route to the same inevitable point.
            I wonder if my father felt this too, right at the end. The quiet relief of not having to pretend anymore.
        <<endif>>
    -> (close your eyes)
        I shut my eyes before the nothing can reach them. As if that changes anything.
        <<if $posSelfPerception > $negSelfPerception>>
            <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
            Behind my eyelids, I see light. Not the star. Something warmer, softer. The afterimage of every small thing that kept me going. Push-ups in a tin can, a puzzle with an alien, a sky I was shown for two seconds.
            The black hole can have the ship. It can't have that.
        <<else>>
            <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
            Behind my eyelids, there's the same darkness. No escape, no difference. Open or closed, the result is the same.
            I've been falling into this my whole life. The mission just gave it a name.
        <<endif>>
<<show BlackHole4>>
My vision goes black. The hum of the ship, the groan of the hull, the pull in my chest, all of it collapses into silence.
For a long time, there is nothing at all.
<<fade_transition 3>>
<<wait 2>>
<<jump StartDay4>>
===
